  grow-from-root: XBART-style root-down tree sampling on the
    provisioned cut-scan kernel; the highest-ceiling large-n item and
    the realistic doorway to any GPU backend. MEMO + KERNEL LANDED
    2026-07-08 (grow-from-root.md; driver benchmarks/kernels/
    grow_from_root.c). Cut-scan measured on M1 Max: seq root scan
    histogram-bound ~13.6 GB/s (not DRAM-bound), scattered-leaf scan
    DRAM/cache-line-bound ~0.7x the 52 GB/s roofline; multiplier
    scan-vs-single-cut ~p on a scattered leaf (10x p=10, 53x p=50),
    ~p/4 root-order. Recommendation: GO on the shared scan primitive
    and grow-from-root as a WARM-START producer (feeds installTrees/
    warm.start, sidesteps validity); NO-GO on shipping it as a
    standalone posterior sampler - the exact-sampler use of the scan
    belongs to frontier 3.1's informed proposal. APPROVED by VD
    2026-07-08 as grow-from-root-warm-start: promote the scan kernel
    into the engine as a shared primitive (constant leaf first,
    reading the leaf model's suffstats), add growTreeFromRoot
    alongside metropolisJumpForTree, wire it to emit a starting
    forest through the installTrees/warm.start surface (user surface
    - bart2 argument vs explicit producer - decided in the plan).
    Shares the scan primitive with frontier item 4, so schedule to
    land the scan once. Queued after the correctness arc (chi fix,
    change-move stage 2, audit blocks 4-7). Review-6 note: the
    promoted scan must be OCCUPANCY-AWARE - the empty-leaf veto
    lives in logLikelihoodForBranch's finite penalty, which a
    scan-based builder never calls; empty-side cuts get zero
    weight in the scan itself, and that contract needs its own
    gate.
  hot-layer-u8: FOLDED into data-ownership's owned container (VD
