  chi-k-runaway: review-6 numerical finding (seed 6), REAL. chi()'s
    scale = Inf DEFAULT (R/model.R:451) is an improper prior; when
    leaves are prior-dominated the k-Gibbs fixed-point factor
    (1 + df/numLeaves) exceeds 1, so legal settings run away: chi
    (100, Inf) deterministically (k -> 1e25+, leaf sd -> 0, the
    forest fits NOTHING, sigma -> marginal sd, NO error); few-tree
    df=1.5 stochastically (k to 1e21 observed). chi(100, scale=2)
    stabilizes at k~21 with a healthy fit. The default 200-tree
    chi(1.5) survives only because data usually overcome the
    1.0037 per-sweep factor. REMEDY IS VD'S CALL: (a) sentinel cap
    on k (~1e6 = leaf sd statistically zero; nearly behavior-
    neutral, catches both modes), (b) finite default scale
    (posterior-changing for every chi user; belongs with
    chi-default-research), (c) warn on updateK + scale=Inf.
    Orchestrator recommends (a) now + fold the default question
    into chi-default-research.
