  missing-incorporate-matrix-interface: sbc-calibration (review 4)
    tier-B finding. The matrix (xy) interface drops NA rows even
    under missing = "incorporate" - the raw branch's complete-cases
    filter runs regardless, so incorporation is only reachable
    through the formula interface (na.action = na.pass). Either make
    the matrix path honor "incorporate" (keep NA rows) or error
    that incorporate requires the formula interface; silent
    dropping contradicts the argument. Small, R validation/docs.
