    equivalence-cf99a00.rds (commit 7b79623, MANIFEST updated).
  tau-slice-stepout-cap: review-6 numerical finding (seed 4), REAL.
    sliceSampleOnce's step-out while loops are uncapped in BOTH
    directions (model.hpp:2299-2301; only shrinkage caps at 1000).
    Step-outs ~ tau/width: >1e5 iterations at tau > ~2.5e5,
    indefinite hang at tau > ~1e8. Reachable legally: empty groups
    draw effects ~N(0, tau^2) with no mean-reversion (mostly-empty
    groupings random-walk tau up); heavy-tail excursions at small
    J; also the cause of the review-3 poison hang and the review-4
    half-Cauchy SBC intractability. Fix: Neal's m cap on both
    directions (~1e4) - never engages in normal runs so all gates
    stay bit-identical; when it engages, shrinkage still samples
    correctly inside the bracket. Small, engine.
  dbarts-results-growth: review-6 architecture debt #2, DECISION,
    window: pre-release. The frozen dbarts_results struct
    (dbarts.h) cannot gain fields - consumers stack-allocate
    against the compiled layout - but NB's r trace, ordinal
    cutpoints, and multinomial per-category fits all need output
    channels. Pick the policy before 1.0-0: a new-named run2 +
    extended results struct, or new-named per-channel getters.
    Related debt #3: flat-format-v2 should become an additive/
    optional-block state format ONCE before the family wave (each
    new family otherwise bumps stateFormatVersion and orphans all
    saved states serially). VD decision.
